{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1766636,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"light-blue-dark_un","paid":0,"title":"OHM MY GOD! IEEExWIE_CRCE","festival_id":521740,"organization_id":17467,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-08T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-30T16:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/ohm-my-god-ieeexwie-crce-crescendo-fr-crce-students-council-1766636","region":"offline","details":"<p>Think you can decode a circuit, make the right engineering decisions, and bring it to life?<\/p>\n<p><strong>OHM MY GOD!<\/strong>, organized by <strong>IEEExWIE CRCE<\/strong> under <strong>CRESCENDO 2026<\/strong>, is a team-based technical electronics challenge designed to test participants&rsquo; circuit understanding, datasheet interpretation, component selection, problem-solving, and hands-on circuit-building skills.<\/p>\n<p>The competition consists of three consecutive phases:<\/p>\n<p><strong>DECODE<\/strong> &ndash; Analyze and complete an incomplete circuit using the provided datasheets.<br \/><strong>DECIDE<\/strong> &ndash; Select suitable components for a given application within a virtual budget.<br \/><strong>BUILD<\/strong> &ndash; Use the selected components to build, test, and demonstrate a working circuit.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Guidelines<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Inter-College Teams:<\/strong> All 3 participants must belong to the <strong>same academic year<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Each team must have <strong>exactly 3 participants<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Registration fee is <strong>\u20b9150 per team<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>The competition is scored out of <strong>100 marks<\/strong> across all three phases.<\/li>\n<li>All required components, datasheets, and basic testing resources will be provided by the organizers.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All participants must follow the official queue\/order assigned by the organizers.<\/li>\n<li>Work beyond the applicable maximum cap shall not be permitted.<\/li>\n<li>The exact completion time for every phase shall be officially recorded.<\/li>\n<li>Teams shall attempt all tasks independently.<\/li>\n<li>Mobile phones, internet access, AI tools, and unauthorized reference material are&nbsp;<br \/>prohibited during active competition.<\/li>\n<li>Only datasheets\/reference material officially provided by the organizers may be used.<\/li>\n<li>Participants shall not communicate answers, circuit connections, or solutions to other&nbsp;<br \/>teams.<\/li>\n<li>Personal electronic components and pre-built circuits\/modules are prohibited.<\/li>\n<li>Only components and equipment authorized by the organizers may be used.<\/li>\n<li>Judges shall not provide technical assistance, hints, or component-selection confirmation.<\/li>\n<li>Phase 2 component selection shall be entirely the responsibility of the participating team.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Selected components shall be carried forward to Phase 3.<\/li>\n<li>Once a team requests an official circuit check in Phase 1 or Phase 3, it will be counted as&nbsp;<br \/>an attempt.<\/li>\n<li>The number of checking attempts shall be determined by the announced participation&nbsp;<br \/>condition.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must follow laboratory and electrical safety instructions.<\/li>\n<li>Judges' decisions regarding circuit correctness and output shall be final.<\/li>\n<li>The judges&rsquo; decision regarding scoring, circuit output, and results will be final.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":"\u20b94,400 prize pool for winning teams based on final rankings, along with winner certificates.","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":33503862,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-06T13:23:37+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-07T23:03:22+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":n